# Claude Code worktrees. NOT ignored until 2026-08-29, which is how
# .claude/worktrees/determined-carson-439745 came to be committed as a GITLINK
# (mode 160000) around the build-265 era. Git reads that entry as a submodule,
# finds no .gitmodules record, and every `actions/checkout` on this repo dies:
#
#   fatal: No url found for submodule path '.claude/worktrees/…' in .gitmodules
#
# That is why the `pages-build-deployment` workflow has failed on every commit
# since at least 2026-08-19. Ignoring the directory stops it happening again; it
# deliberately does NOT untrack the existing gitlink (see the note below).
.claude/worktrees/

# ── Session handoff docs are NEVER committed ────────────────────────────────
# A handoff is a snapshot of one session's state. Committed, it goes stale in
# days and then actively misleads: the root HANDOFF.md sat tracked from
# 2026-08-18 to 2026-09-01 telling every cold tab "read it before touching
# anything" while describing build 457 and an unmerged branch, long after
# builds 472-476 had merged. That was its THIRD staleness incident — see
# "refresh HANDOFF.md — it was 5 weeks and 41 builds stale" (#284) and
# "three of its claims were wrong" (3f9b842) — and it was an OPEN finding in
# docs/ia-audit-2026-07 the whole time. Write handoffs OUTSIDE the repo and
# hand over the absolute path. Pinned by e2e/noStaleHandoff.test.mjs.
HANDOFF.md
HANDOFF-*.md
*-HANDOFF.md
